1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:09.700
A modern car can be stopped by a component smaller than your fingernail.

2
00:00:09.700 --> 00:00:19.400
A phone, a hospital scanner, a power grid, a factory: all of them depend on chips that most people will never see.

3
00:00:19.400 --> 00:00:49.400
Now imagine needing those chips while the factories that make them are concentrated far beyond your borders.

4
00:00:49.400 --> 00:01:06.350
So what does it take to make one?

5
00:01:06.350 --> 00:01:23.300
It begins with something almost impossible to see.

6
00:01:23.300 --> 00:01:29.275
One of the central ideas is photolithography.

7
00:01:29.275 --> 00:01:35.250
Think of shining light through a stencil onto a surface coated with a light-sensitive material.

8
00:01:35.250 --> 00:01:41.225
The exposed pattern can guide later processing steps.

9
00:01:41.225 --> 00:01:47.200
In a chip factory, this process is repeated with extraordinary alignment and control.

10
00:01:47.200 --> 00:02:16.600
But the pattern is only part of the challenge.

11
00:02:16.600 --> 00:02:22.160
Next comes layering.

12
00:02:22.160 --> 00:02:27.720
A chip is not one flat drawing.

13
00:02:27.720 --> 00:02:33.280
It is built through repeated processes that create and connect tiny electronic structures.

14
00:02:33.280 --> 00:02:38.840
Think of a city where roads, tunnels, wires and junctions must line up across many levels.

15
00:02:38.840 --> 00:02:44.400
If one critical connection fails, the finished device may not work.

16
00:02:44.400 --> 00:02:50.800
And even a completed wafer is not the end.

17
00:02:50.800 --> 00:02:57.200
Chips must be separated, connected, packaged and tested.

18
00:02:57.200 --> 00:03:03.600
Packaging protects the device and provides connections to the outside world.

19
00:03:03.600 --> 00:03:10.000
It is technically demanding, but it is not the same process as fabricating advanced transistors on a wafer.

20
00:03:10.000 --> 00:03:15.560
India is trying to strengthen several parts of this chain.

21
00:03:15.560 --> 00:03:21.120
According to a government press note from this year, twelve manufacturing units are approved.

22
00:03:21.120 --> 00:03:26.680
Nine of them are for assembly, test and packaging.

23
00:03:26.680 --> 00:03:32.240
Three are fabrication units.

24
00:03:32.240 --> 00:03:37.800
Five units have begun commercial production, while other major projects remain under development.

25
00:03:37.800 --> 00:03:43.580
Here is a fictional scenario.

26
00:03:43.580 --> 00:03:49.360
A factory receives a perfect chip design, but a critical processing tool is unavailable.

27
00:03:49.360 --> 00:03:55.140
The design cannot simply become a working wafer.

28
00:03:55.140 --> 00:04:00.920
Another factory can package chips, but it cannot automatically replace the missing fabrication step.

29
00:04:00.920 --> 00:04:06.700
The chain is only as strong as the capability it lacks.

30
00:04:06.700 --> 00:04:14.750
Advanced equipment, materials, process expertise, yields and a reliable supplier ecosystem take years to build.

31
00:04:14.750 --> 00:04:22.800
Announcing a plant is not the same as mastering every generation of chip technology.

32
00:04:22.800 --> 00:04:52.800
But building capability changes the choices available to a country, and to the companies that depend on it.
